WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
I’ve been making videos for a lot of years,&nbsp;
and whether it's for Vox or The New York Times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.720
or for the channel, music is easily one of the&nbsp;
biggest things that changes how a video feels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.820
Music like this... If you've been around for&nbsp;
a while, you've definitely heard me say things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:21.300
like this before... That thing that inspires me is&nbsp;
music. So I started working with this guy. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.760
a good sound. This is Tom. Tom Fox. We've been&nbsp;
collaborating since 2018 and now five years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.140
Tom is the full time composer here in the&nbsp;
studio. He makes the music for every one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.640
videos. Why does a small independent journalism&nbsp;
production studio on YouTube need a full time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.320
composer? That’s absurd! Yes, it is absurd and&nbsp;
it's completely necessary. And it is what makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.420
these videos shine. From the Europe videos to the&nbsp;
Putin videos, to the videos about Doritos. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.040
one of these has a different tone and feel because&nbsp;
we crafted music that fits for that story. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.640
there's now a place where you can listen to&nbsp;
this music. It is called The Listening Room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.940
it's totally free up on YouTube right&nbsp;
now. You can listen to it while you work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.141
while you study, while you work out...&nbsp;
See you in The Listening Room, everyone!

